(AUTHORITY: Kalin v. Campbell, 2014 BCCA 441 \(PAGE 2 OF 3\)) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 10 Tf
54 698 Td
(Fiduciary Duty of Accounting & Commercial Sensitivity) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 9.5 Tf
16 TL
54 665 Td
([4] Where a fiduciary or contractual duty of accounting is pleaded in relation to designated joint venture funds, the) Tj
T*
(    underlying bank statements and source transaction vouchers are fundamentally material. A party claiming an accounting) Tj
T*
(    is not required to accept their opponent's self-selected summaries. Transparency is the bedrock of the disclosure process.) Tj
T*
([5] Nor does a generalized claim of 'commercial sensitivity' preclude disclosure. Where sensitive proprietary terms exist,) Tj
T*
(    the appropriate mechanism is a confidentiality undertaking or protective order, not an outright refusal to produce.) Tj
T*
([6] Having regard to the proportionality principles in Rule 1-3, the production of electronic bank records presents negligible) Tj
T*
(    cost or burden to the party holding them.) Tj
T*
([7] The appeal is allowed. The respondents shall deliver a verified supplementary list and produce the bank records within 14 days.) Tj
ET
endstream
endobj
